// Phorensic OS — Complete Source Tree
// =====================================
//
// Current status: Bootstrapping / Observed
// Build state: Framebuffer boot screen operational
// Compiler state: Rust frontend (lex/parse/check) + backend scaffold (PHIR → x86-64 → ELF64)
// OS state: Boot path working (ASM → GOP → StatusScreen → Canvas → Console → Shell)
// Verification state: Spec/model tests present for checker; no full executable court yet
//
// Build with:    phorc build [file.ph] [output.o]        # single-file compilation to ELF64
// Build all:     phorc build --all                        # planned
// Test with:     phorc test [file.ph]                     # planned
// Verify with:   phorc verify [file.ph]                   # planned
// Court with:    phor_court --session=...                 # planned
// Package with:  phor_pkg --verify --store                # planned
//
// Codebase statistics (approximate):
//   Total .phor files: 294
//   Total .phor lines: ~318k
//   Total lines:       ~364k
//   .asm files:        4
//   .asm lines:        ~4k
//
// All code follows Phorensic language specification:
//   - no_std, no_alloc, no_unsafe core
//   - affine capabilities (no duplication)
//   - generation-tagged handles
//   - fixed-capacity collections only
//   - bounded loops everywhere
//   - explicit effect declarations
//   - typed errors with stable diagnostic codes
//   - residual emission on all state changes
//   - trusted blocks with rationale only
//
// Compiler architecture:
//   .ph source → lex → parse → check → lower(PHIR) → x86-64 select → encode → ELF64 .o + receipts
//
// Current phorc capabilities:
//   ✓ Lexer: full token set for Phorensic language
//   ✓ Parser: function/struct/enum/type/package declarations, expressions, statements
//   ✓ Checker: symbol table, type checking, capability tracking, effect checking, loop bounds
//   ✓ PHIR: mid-level IR with basic blocks, ops, types
//   ✓ x86-64 codegen: prologue/epilogue, binops, store/load (via iced-x86)
//   ✓ ELF64 object writer: .text/.data/.bss sections, symbols (via object crate)
//   ✓ Receipts: byte attribution map, function receipts, compilation residuals
//   ✓ Example compilation: 44/44 .phor files compile with 0 errors
//   ✓ Interactive shell with PS/2 keyboard input
//   ✓ UART serial driver with capability model
//   ✓ Canvas rendering primitives ported to .phor
//   ✓ JIT/dialect cage porting engine demo
//   △ Checker not yet integrated with all lowering stages
//   △ Backend: register allocation, memory operands, call ABI still minimal
//
// Boot path target:
//   UEFI GOP framebuffer → GUI compositor → window manager → status panel → inspector
//   (see docs/FORENSIC_OS_VISION.md, src/boot/, src/gui/)
//
